## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design end-to-end CAPA for privacy-policy drift in a multi-tenant, partner‑integrated data plane. Requires data modeling, lifecycle management, API surfaces, observability, and rollout safety.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model including lineage and policy versions
- Region/tenant-aware metrics
- Lifecycle state machine and RCA templates
- Canary rollout and rollback safeguards

## Code Example
```javascript
type CAPA = {
  id: string;
  tenantId: string;
  region: string;
  policyVersion: string;
  evidenceRefs: string[];
  dataLineage: string;
  rootCause?: string;
  correctiveAction?: string;
  containmentStatus: 'detected'|'investigating'|'contained'|'verified'|'closed';
  timestamps: { detected: string; updated?: string; closed?: string };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the canary rollout for a policy upgrade in this scenario?
- What data access controls and retention would you enforce during CAPA investigations?

